opentune-ols
============

This crate reads WinOLS `.ols` project files (the proprietary EVC/WinOLS project
container: ROM image + project map/table definitions + metadata).

The `.ols` container and record layout implemented here — the 24-byte header and
"WinOLS File" signature, the MFC CArchive-style length-prefixed metadata fields,
the version-directory anchor and record sizing, and the WinOLS 5 map-record /
axis field walk — was learned from the STRUCTURE described by two open-source
GPL-3.0 readers and re-implemented from scratch:

    ZedSuite — https://github.com/LeZed97/ZedSuite
      (src-tauri/src/ols_import.rs, ols_maps.rs)
    romHEX14-community — https://github.com/ctabuyo/romHEX14-community
      (src/io/ols/*.cpp), cross-referenced by ZedSuite

Both are licensed GPL-3.0, which is compatible with OpenTune
(GPL-3.0-or-later). This crate is NOT a line-for-line translation or a vendored
copy: it uses its own types, its own module decomposition, its own reader and
validation, and shares no source text with either project. The on-disk byte
order and offsets follow the format those readers document so that real WinOLS
files decode consistently.

SCOPE / HONESTY
---------------
WinOLS `.ols` is only partly a plaintext format. This crate:

  * recovers the plaintext parts — header, identification metadata, version
    directory, the raw (uncompressed) ROM image of each saved version, and, for
    WinOLS 5 containers (format version >= 800), the project's map definitions;
  * does NOT decode WinOLS 4.x (format < 800) map-record layouts (ROM still
    extracts; maps come back empty with a warning);
  * does NOT decrypt encrypted / "protected" WinOLS projects (they fail with a
    "not a container" error because the plaintext layout is absent);
  * does NOT recover WinOLS internal checksum-region definitions (not present in
    the metadata this parser reads — reported as a warning, never fabricated);
  * flags, rather than fabricates, anything with no OpenTune equivalent
    (64-bit cell types, non-linear scaling).

No `.ols` files are shipped with this crate. See LICENSE (GPL-3.0-or-later) in
the repository root for the full license text.
